TASK T005: let the review workflow accept configured custom review dimensions after the four canonical ones.
FILE: .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml
EDITS (apply all, literally; anchors are text, not line numbers):
1. The input line that starts `  review_dimensions: "[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability] - Dimensions to check. Default: all."` becomes:
  review_dimensions: "[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability|custom names] - Dimensions to check. The four canonical dimensions are correctness, security, traceability and maintainability; any other name is a custom dimension, reviewed after the canonical four in configured order. Default: all."
2. In step `step_order_dimensions`, its `algorithm` line `          3. If review_dimensions != "all", filter to only requested dimensions` becomes:
          3. If review_dimensions != "all", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order
3. In step `step_normalize_review_dimensions`:
   a. Under its `outputs:` list, after the `review_dimensions_json` line, add two lines at the same indentation:
          - review_dimensions_list: "The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '"
          - dimension_coverage_seed: "JSON object mapping the canonical four, then each configured custom dimension, to false"
   b. In its `normalize:` block, after the line `            - ["correctness"] → ["correctness"]` add:
            - "correctness,performance" → ["correctness","performance"]
   c. Replace the line `          Every element MUST be one of the four canonical dimension names.` with:
          Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.
4. In step `step_create_findings_registry`, in its `content:` JSON string, replace exactly `"dimensionCoverage":{"correctness":false,"security":false,"traceability":false,"maintainability":false}` with `"dimensionCoverage":{dimension_coverage_seed}`. Change nothing else on that line.
5. In the `render_prompt_pack:` block, under `variables:`, after the line `              review_focus_block: "{review_focus_block}"` add:
              review_dimensions_list: "{review_dimensions_list}"
6. In the top-level `review_dimensions:` table near the end of the file: change its `note:` value from `"All 4 default review dimensions with priority ordering"` to `"The four canonical review dimensions in priority order; each configured custom dimension follows them under the custom rubric row"`, and after the `maintainability` row add, at the same indentation:
      - { priority: 5, name: "<custom>", checks: "A configured custom dimension: review the target for the property its name states, under the shared P0-P2 doctrine. It follows the canonical four in configured order and is not required for severity coverage." }
